openmediavault-filebrowser-quantum (8.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: FileBrowser Quantum management plugin for
    OpenMediaVault 8.x.
    - Settings: image tag, image variant (full/slim), web port, the
      data shared folder (config, SQLite database and cache) and the
      source shared folder that is exposed for browsing.
    - The Docker container is registered in the openmediavault-compose
      plugin on save (Compose.setFile), so it follows the Compose
      plugin conventions (<compose shared folder>/filebrowserquantum/)
      and shows up in the Compose web UI (Services -> Compose ->
      Files / Services) where it can also be inspected, edited,
      started and stopped. The plugin does not render the stack files
      itself.
    - The data and source folders are referenced through the Compose
      placeholder '${{ sf:"<name>" }}', so a changed shared folder path
      is resolved by the Compose plugin on deploy.
    - A minimal config.yaml (source mount point /srv) is created in the
      data shared folder on first Apply and never overwritten
      afterwards, so the web interface works out of the box.
    - Live status: container state, running image version, latest
      upstream release for the configured channel and update
      detection, log viewer and rendered compose file preview. The
      upstream release is read from the GitHub releases feed, with the
      (rate limited) REST API as a fallback for networks where the
      feed host is unreachable.
    - Start/Stop/Restart/Upgrade run as background tasks (through the
      Compose plugin helper omv-compose-run) with live output.
    - Simplified and Traditional Chinese translations included.

